WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.053 --> 00:00:04.705
Here's the part people get wrong most often.

2
00:00:04.705 --> 00:00:09.466
You don't set access on the course itself. This Library access box is a mirror.

3
00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:11.635
It reports what MemberPress decides.

4
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:17.994
Access is managed under Library, Access Groups. Live is what members have now.

5
00:00:17.994 --> 00:00:21.122
Draft is where your changes wait until you publish.

6
00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:30.135
An Access Group is a package of content.

7
00:00:30.135 --> 00:00:33.934
Open a group, and under What this group unlocks, tick the course.

8
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.752
Each group lists the memberships that include it. Save draft keeps your change.

9
00:00:44.752 --> 00:00:46.843
Saving never changes member access.

10
00:00:48.776 --> 00:00:54.033
You can also tick groups from a MemberPress membership, in its Library Access Groups box.

11
00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.923
That saves to the draft as well.

12
00:00:58.775 --> 00:01:03.410
When you're ready, preview the check first. Publishing checks every current member.

13
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.597
If anyone would lose access, nothing is published, and you see exactly who.

14
00:01:10.419 --> 00:01:15.478
Once it's live, the course's access box reads Protected by MemberPress and names the group.

15
00:01:15.478 --> 00:01:17.145
That's how you know it worked.
